{
  "title": "Modified component ProfileForm to reset after a save",
  "context": [
    "The account form kept the name and email it first loaded as its starting values, also after a save. A successful save now replaces those starting values with the name and email the server sent back. The two fields show what the server stored, not what the user typed. A failed save leaves the form as the user left it.",
    "",
    "## Overview",
    "",
    "- **When** a user saves the profile form and the server stores a name or an email that differs from the typed text, **then** [the two fields show the name and email the server returned](code:src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx#L15).",
    "- **When** the server returns the name and email as the user typed them, **then** nothing changes on the page.",
    "- **When** the save fails, **then** nothing changes.",
    "- **When** a user submits a name of one character, **then** nothing changes.",
    "",
    "## Implementation",
    "",
    "**`src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx`**",
    "",
    "- Modified [`<ProfileForm />` to read `reset` from the result of `useForm()`](code:src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx#L9).",
    "- Modified [`onSubmit()` to pass an `onSuccess` callback to `saveProfile()`](code:src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx#L14-16), which calls `reset()` with the profile the server returned."
  ],
  "diff": [
    "diff --git a/src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx b/src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx",
    "--- a/src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx",
    "+++ b/src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx",
    "@@ -9 +9 @@ export function ProfileForm({ profile }: { profile: Profile }) {",
    "-  const { register, handleSubmit, formState } = useForm<Profile>({",
    "+  const { register, handleSubmit, formState, reset } = useForm<Profile>({",
    "@@ -15 +15 @@ export function ProfileForm({ profile }: { profile: Profile }) {",
    "-    saveProfile(values)",
    "+    saveProfile(values, { onSuccess: (savedProfile) => reset(savedProfile) })"
  ],
